{"name":"Minsk","hex":"#3e3267","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Minsk","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The capital city of Belarus.","The Belarusian government."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Minsk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Minsk","blocks":[{"text":"Minsk is the capital and largest city of Belarus, located on the Svislach and the now subterranean Nyamiha rivers. As the capital, Minsk has a special administrative status in Belarus and is the administrative centre of Minsk region and Minsk district. As of 2026, it has a population of about two million, making Minsk the 11th-most populous city in Europe. Minsk is one of the administrative capitals of the Commonwealth of Independent States (CIS) and the Eurasian Economic Union (EAEU)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/View_of_Minsk_%28180819%29_09.jpg/330px-View_of_Minsk_%28180819%29_09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minsk","wikidata":"Q2280"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Miensk_-_Ratu%C5%A1a.jpg/500px-Miensk_-_Ratu%C5%A1a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Miensk_-_Ratu%C5%A1a.jpg/1280px-Miensk_-_Ratu%C5%A1a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Miensk_-_Ratu%C5%A1a.jpg/500px-Miensk_-_Ratu%C5%A1a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMiensk_-_Ratu%C5%A1a.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/%D0%9C%D1%96%D0%BD%D1%81%D0%BA._%D0%9F%D0%B5%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BF%D0%B0%D1%9E%D0%BB%D0%B0%D1%9E%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%8F_%D1%86%D0%B0%D1%80%D0%BA%D0%B2%D0%B0_2.jpg/500px-%D0%9C%D1%9